@startuml
title Help With COVID Session and Task Workflow - System Architecture

left to right direction
skinparam componentStyle rectangle

actor "Authenticated App User" as AppUser
actor "End User" as EndUser
actor "Deployment/Config Operator" as Operator

cloud "External User Channel\n(Text/Call)" as Channel

node "Environment" as Env {
  artifact "Env Vars:\n- FIREBASE_AUTH_DOMAIN\n- FIREBASE_DATABASE_URL\n- FIREBASE_PROJECT_ID\n- FIREBASE_PUBLIC_API_KEY" as EnvVars <<env>>
}

package "Frontend (Next.js)" as Frontend {
  component "Frontend App" as FE_App
  component "Frontend Form" as FE_Form
  component "Session Handler" as FE_SessionHandler
  package "Next.js API Routes" as FE_APIs {
    component "/api/login [POST]" as API_Login
    component "/api/logout [POST]" as API_Logout
  }
  component "Runtime Config" as FE_Config <<config>>
}

package "Middleware" as MW {
  component "Session Middleware\n(server-side session support)" as MW_Session
  component "Task Middleware\n- Address -> Neighborhood\n- Service-area decision" as MW_Task
}

package "Backend (Firebase Functions)" as Backend {
  component "Task Handler\n(OnFleet Task Creation)" as BE_TaskHandler
}

cloud "Firebase Auth (Client SDK)" as FirebaseAuth
cloud "Firebase Admin Token Verification" as FirebaseAdmin
cloud "OnFleet API" as OnFleet

' Operators provide environment configuration
Operator --> EnvVars : Provide env values\n(CON-001)
EnvVars --> FE_Config : Map to runtime config\n(FR-008, NFR-003)

' Runtime config consumed by frontend
FE_Config --> FE_App
FE_Config --> FE_SessionHandler

' User interactions
AppUser --> FE_App : Use application\n(UI-003)
EndUser --> FE_Form : Submit help-task request\n(UI-001)

' Session handler flows
FE_App --> FE_SessionHandler : Trigger session establishment/logout\n(UI-003)

FE_SessionHandler --> FirebaseAuth : user.getIdToken()\n(FR-001, DR-001, DR-002)

FE_SessionHandler --> API_Login : POST /api/login\nBody: { token }\n(FR-001, SI-001, CI-001, NFR-001, NFR-002)
note on link
- JSON body contains "token"
- Content-Type: application/json
- Same-origin credentials
end note

FE_SessionHandler --> API_Logout : POST /api/logout\n(FR-002, SI-002, CI-002, NFR-002)
note on link
- No request body required
- Same-origin credentials
end note

' API routes execute with session middleware
MW_Session <.. API_Login : Executes with session support\n(SI-004, FR-006)
MW_Session <.. API_Logout : Executes with session support\n(SI-004)

' Login API internal responsibilities
API_Login --> FirebaseAdmin : Verify ID token\n(FR-005, SI-003)
API_Login --> MW_Session : Store decoded token + token\n(FR-006)
note right of API_Login
- Validate request body; 400 if missing (FR-003)
- Extract token from req.body (FR-004)
- Verify Firebase ID token (FR-005)
- Write decoded token and token to session (FR-006)
- Return 200 with success JSON incl. decoded token (FR-007)
end note

' Logout API behavior (implicit session clear)
note right of API_Logout
- Tear down session on logout (SI-002)
end note

' Task workflow
FE_Form --> MW_Task : Task request\n(CI-003, FR-010)
Channel --> MW_Task : Task request from external channel\n(UI-002, FR-010)

note right of MW_Task
- Process address -> neighborhood (FR-011)
- Determine operated service area (FR-011)
- Forward eligible requests to backend (CI-004)
end note

MW_Task --> BE_TaskHandler : Eligible task request\n(CI-004, FR-012)
BE_TaskHandler --> OnFleet : Create task\n(SI-005, FR-012)

' Non-functional and run modes
note bottom of Frontend
Run modes (FR-009, CON-006):
- Both servers
- Frontend only
- Backend only
end note

note bottom of FE_Config
Firebase runtime config (FR-008):
- FIREBASE_AUTH_DOMAIN
- FIREBASE_DATABASE_URL
- FIREBASE_PROJECT_ID
- FIREBASE_PUBLIC_API_KEY
end note

@enduml
